WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:01.290
- Welcome back y'all.

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.520
I love finding great stories

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.290
from social media and
sharing them right here.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:05.592
This is "What I'm liking".

00:00:05.592 --> 00:00:08.040
(upbeat fun music)
(audience clap)

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.590
Firefighters put their lives
on the line all the time

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:13.650
but in Illinois, a group of
firefighters go a step further.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.510
It's called "Project Fire Buddies",

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:18.600
and the firefighter led
organization help sick children

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.790
with special visits and resources.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.430
They organize toy
drives, sponsor families.

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:25.200
They've even actually
arranged get well videos

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.690
from celebrities like Dwayne
Johnson and Jack Black.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:28.710
So cool.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:31.260
Kurt DeGroot of the "Oak
Forest Fire Department"

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.620
founded the organization and
he watches on "NBC 5 Chicago".

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:35.760
He's joining us now.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.440
Everybody say hi to Kurt.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.315
What's up, Kurt?
(audience clapping)

00:00:39.315 --> 00:00:40.148
- Hey, Kelly.

00:00:40.148 --> 00:00:43.350
It it's an absolute honor to
to be out here and to meet you.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.340
Thank you so much.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.600
- Oh man. It's an honor to have you.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.010
First of all, thank you for your service

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.620
as a firefighter, first and foremost.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.290
And also thank you for
taking it a step further

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:53.520
and caring so much about these people.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:54.353
So this is amazing.

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:55.890
Where did you get this idea?

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.680
- So, I've been a firefighter
paramedic for 21 years now

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.810
and some of the toughest
calls that we go on is

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:04.650
for children, especially
children that are critically ill.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.762
So it's especially hard because these kids

00:01:06.762 --> 00:01:09.180
when when we go there,
they're excited to see us

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:10.710
but you can see the pain that they're in

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.990
and the struggle that
they're going through.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:16.170
There was one child in
particular that, I mean

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:18.635
we would go there, transport
'em several different times

00:01:18.635 --> 00:01:21.517
and I remember asking the family,

00:01:21.517 --> 00:01:23.130
"Hey. is there any way we could stop by

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.030
and hang out sometime?

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:26.100
Maybe play some air hockey?"

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:26.933
We did.

00:01:26.933 --> 00:01:27.766
It was great.

00:01:27.766 --> 00:01:29.310
We saw how much the child loved it,

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:30.990
how much the family loved it

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.670
and words started to spread around town.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:33.780
We found some more children

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:35.940
in the area that were critically ill.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:36.990
We started to do it there

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.960
and spread all across social media.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.640
And now I'm proud to say that we're

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:44.190
in 35 different departments
across several states.

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:48.155
- Wow. Look what you started;
that ripple effect, man.

00:01:48.155 --> 00:01:49.193
It's not just visits though.

00:01:49.193 --> 00:01:51.720
So what else do you provide?

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.910
- So we're firefighters,
so of course we're gonna,

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:55.920
we're gonna be loud, we're gonna be proud.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.500
We line the streets up with fire vehicles.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:01:59.700
We shut down the street,

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:02.910
we turn the sirens on, blare the horn.

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:05.280
We wanna make sure that the world stops

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.110
and knows that we're there for that child

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:10.530
and they're part of our crew
and they're part of our family.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:14.190
You know, we've got given
tons of toys and gifts

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:17.130
and experiences through different
kind of sporting events;

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:19.530
once in a lifetime experiences.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:21.180
Sometimes with the older
kids it's a little tough

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:23.252
'cause the firetrucks aren't
so cool for them, you know?

00:02:23.252 --> 00:02:25.830
But, we make do, we figure it out

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:28.560
and that's where those
experiences really come in.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.800
We've had a lot of help
from Dwayne the Rock Johnson

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.293
you know, Gal Gadot, Jack Black.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.440
Robert Downey Jr's helped us, you know

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.240
and then, you know, since the start of it

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.790
we've helped over a
hundred different families

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:44.879
and we've raised just under $500,000.

00:02:44.879 --> 00:02:45.712
- Wow. It's truly incredible, Kurt.

00:02:45.712 --> 00:02:48.870
(audience clapping)

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:49.830
Thank you so much.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:51.300
You're such a brave heart

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.010
and such a cool heart
and sharing it with us.

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:55.140
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.228
- [Kurt] Oh, that's incredible.

00:02:56.228 --> 00:02:58.740
- And that's not all Kurt.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:01.020
Our season long partner
"Pilot Pen Makers of G2",

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:02.880
the go-to pen in the "Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:03.840
love what you're doing.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:07.557
So they're giving "Project Fire
Buddies" a thousand dollars.

00:03:07.557 --> 00:03:08.789
(audience cheers)

00:03:08.789 --> 00:03:10.157
- Oh my, oh my.

00:03:10.157 --> 00:03:12.476
Thank you so much.

00:03:12.476 --> 00:03:13.309
This is awesome.

00:03:13.309 --> 00:03:14.651
- Absolutely. Thank you, Kurt.

00:03:14.651 --> 00:03:15.870
Have a good day.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:17.160
Thank you tll our guests this hour.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.100
Joshua Jackson, Christine
Cole, Kristen Kish

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.360
as well as Leanne and Kelly.

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:22.193
Y'all have a great day.

00:03:22.193 --> 00:03:23.810
And if it's not, try and change.

